  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently the tested bit rate limit for audio streaming into VRC via AVPro is 320 kbps. Past that the decoder breaks in the game. 320 is great for stereo but when streaming 5.1 (6 discreet channels) there is a significant degradation of audio quality because the 320kbps is divided by the number of AAC channels being streamed. If it where possible to push higher bit rates like 620 kbps and higher it would greatly increase immersive playback capability.\nI believe that the issue is a limitation in Windows Media Foundation? but there is no reference to bit rate ceiling in their docs. I am able to stream higher bit rate and receive it via other decoders.\n\n\n\nUpdate: There is a partial fix to this, If you stream in MPEG you can push the bit rates, in other formats it breaks.",
